CPU vs. GPU
    CPU: Computer Processor (Central Processing Unit)
        Made by Intel and AMD etc. 
    GPU: Graphics Proccessing Unit
        Made to process pictures (notable in computers made for Video Games)
          The original GPU hardware is very powerful and can build very large neural                 netowrks or very large deep learning algoithms. 
        Sold by Nvidia, but Google and Qualcomm are making its own TPUs which are                  specialized hardware that are made to handle large neural networks. 
        
Cloud vs. On-Premises Deployment
  Cloud Deployments refer to renting compute servers from Amazon's AWS, Microsoft's Euro,    or Google's GCP in order to use someone else's service to do YOUR computaion
  
  On-Prem deployment means buying your own compute service and running the service locally
  
  Edge Deployment: Put processor right where the data is collected (in a car) so you can     process the data quickly and make decision (stop car) without waiting for the data to      go to data center and be processed there. 
    
